{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB 5% cap on Berkeley Annual General Adjustment","requirement":"For fully covered units, the annual rent increase (Annual General Adjustment) may not exceed 5%, even if the Rent Ordinance formula produces a higher figure.","key_value":"5% cap on AGA","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units include most multifamily units built before 1980 and government-owned or subsidized units (e.g. Section 8, Shelter Plus Care); partially covered units include most single-family homes, condominiums and post-1980 new construction.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1980","built_after":null,"date_basis":"certificate_of_occupancy","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Fully covered units; government-subsidized units newly covered; shared kitchen or bath units exempt only if the landlord did not live on the property at the start of the tenancy"},"exemptions":"Units exempt from the Rent Ordinance; single-family homes and condominiums are only partially covered. Banked (unused) AGAs from previous years may still raise rent above 5% to reach the rent ceiling.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":"Whether a unit is fully or partially covered depends on whether federal law, state law, or administrative regulation exempts it from Berkeley's rent control provisions.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB changes to Berkeley just cause eviction rules","requirement":"Tenants in fully or partially covered units may be evicted only for just cause: nonpayment eviction requires at least one month's Fair Market Rent in debt, and tenants cannot be evicted for refusing to sign a similar lease. Owner move-in relocation assistance is adjusted annually.","key_value":"1 month's Fair Market Rent minimum rental debt","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance. Landlords must file eviction notices, notices to quit and eviction lawsuits with the Rent Board within three business days of service.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Fully and partially covered rental units; units exempt from the Rent Ordinance are outside just cause"},"exemptions":"Units exempt from the Rent Ordinance, including a unit where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with a landlord who did not live on the property at the start of the tenancy.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
